This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The overarching task (spanning this entire long session) has been an iterative InstUI-alignment refactor of the pantoken monorepo's docs CDN picker (`docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CdnPicker.vue`, `IconPicker.vue`, `CdnPickerPage.vue`, and eventually a new `WebComponentsPicker.vue`), all tracked on branch `cdn-picker-instui-refactor` against PR #75. The user has driven this through many rounds of direct feedback and bug reports, each time reviewed/implemented/verified/committed before moving to the next.

   The most recent, still-unimplemented request (the reason for this summary) is:
   > "the output code snippet can be switched to the native vitepress md codefence which will include syntax highlighting and a built-in copy button."

   This refers specifically to `docs/.vitepress/theme/components/PickerOutput.vue` — the shared component (used by `CdnPicker.vue`, `IconPicker.vue`, and `WebComponentsPicker.vue`) that renders the dynamically-generated output snippet in a `<pre><code>` block with a hand-rolled copy button. The user wants this switched to VitePress's native markdown code-fence rendering to get Shiki syntax highlighting and VitePress's built-in copy-button behavior, instead of the custom implementation.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Vue 3 `<script setup>` SFCs, `computed()`/`ref()`/`watch()` reactivity, Vue's `:checked`/`.indeterminate` DOM property binding (no native `v-model` for indeterminate — must be imperatively set via a template `ref` + `watchEffect`).
   - InstUI/pantoken CSS component system: `.instui-*` prefixed classes with `-modifier` key-value convention, `.instui-view` (View primitive with `-background-*`/`-shadow-*`/`-border-*` modifiers), `.instui-tabs` (`.list`/`.tab`/`.panel` parts, `-variant-secondary` for "folder" underline tabs), `.instui-context-view` (popover with CSS anchor positioning via `position-anchor`/`anchor-name`, needs `-placement-*` modifier to engage), `.instui-checkbox`, `.instui-button` (`-icon-<name>` modifier for leading glyphs, `-shape-circle`/`-color-tertiary` etc.), `.instui-input-group` (`.before`/`.after` icon slots), `.instui-heading` (`-variant-label -border-top` used as a text+rule divider substitute), the icon-glyph CSS system (`.-icon-<name>` classes + `--instui-icon-<name>` mask data-URI custom properties, in `formats/components/generated/icons.css`, globally imported in `docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts`).
   - VitePress internals: `useData()`/`useRoute()`/`useRouter()` composables, the client-side SPA router's `hashchange`/`popstate` handling (`location.hash =` fires a real `hashchange` and creates a history entry; `history.replaceState()` does neither), VitePress's dark-mode `.dark` class on `<html>` + `color-scheme` CSS property + `light-dark()` CSS function for token resolution, VitePress's markdown-it pipeline and Shiki-based syntax highlighting (the CURRENT research topic), the default theme's code-block copy-button mechanism.
   - Build tooling: Vite's `build()` API in library mode (`build.lib.entry`/`formats: ["iife"]`), Rollup's inability to code-split `iife`/`umd` output (confirmed via direct testing, not just claimed), ES module static reachability analysis and why importing ANY named export from a module with top-level side-effecting code (like an auto-invoked `register()` call) forces that side effect to run and everything it references to be bundled.
   - jsDelivr CDN: `/combine/` endpoint for concatenating multiple small files into one HTTP response (works for both CSS and, as leveraged here, self-invoking IIFE JS files executed in order).
   - Deep-linking pattern: URL hash as a flat `URLSearchParams`-style key-value store, read once at component setup via `readHashParam`, written via `writeHashParam(key, value, defaultValue)` which omits the key entirely when it matches the default (so an untouched picker leaves no trace in the URL).
   - Changesets workflow (`@pantoken/docs` patch, `@pantoken/web-components` minor), `vpr ready` gate (lint/typecheck/full test suite/changeset-coverage/duplication-audit/snyk/markdownlint), commitlint rules (subject must not start with an all-caps word).
   - Node ESM module evaluation semantics: importing a named export from a module executes the ENTIRE module including top-level side effects, which was the root cause of the "all per-element files came out 2.5MB" bug.

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **`docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CdnPickerPage.vue`**: Added page title (`<h1 class="instui-heading -level-h1 -variant-title-page">{{ t.title }}</h1>`, reusing frontmatter string "CDN Picker"), replaced fake button tabs with real `.instui-tabs` (`list`/`tab`/`panel` structure), added third "Web components" tab, added deep-linking for `activeTab` via `tab` hash param (`initialTab`/`watch(activeTab, ...)`).
   - **`docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CdnPicker.vue`**: Card → `-background-primary -shadow-resting` (no border). Search → `.instui-input-group` with `-icon-search`. Copy button → `-icon-copy`. Token-sheet radio removed (always lean). Base/Utilities moved into the checkbox grid as first entries (checked by default), each with an info-popover button (`-icon-info -shape-circle -color-tertiary`, unique `anchor-name`/`position-anchor` per popover: `--cdn-picker-base-anchor`/`--cdn-picker-utilities-anchor`) opening `.instui-context-view -placement-bottom` popovers with accurate blurb text sourced verbatim from `formats/components/src/rules/base.ts`'s JSDoc `@summary`. "All components" moved to first row of the grid. Extracted to use `useIndeterminateCheckbox` composable and `PickerOutput.vue`. Deep-linking via `c_sel`/`c_base`/`c_util`/`c_fmt`/`c_q` hash params. **Most recent fix** (tri-state bug):
     ```ts
     const allComponentsSelected = computed(
       () => components.length > 0 && selected.value.size === components.length,
     );
     const allSelected = computed(
       () => allComponentsSelected.value && includeBase.value && includeUtilities.value,
     );
     const someSelected = computed(
       () =>
         !allSelected.value && (selected.value.size > 0 || includeBase.value || includeUtilities.value),
     );
     const allCheckboxEl = useIndeterminateCheckbox(someSelected);
     watch(selected, (s) => {
       const value = allComponentsSelected.value ? "all" : [...s].join(",");
       writeHashParam("c_sel", value, "");
     });

     function toggleAll(checked: boolean): void {
       selected.value = checked ? new Set(components.map((c) => c.name)) : new Set();
       includeBase.value = checked;
       includeUtilities.value = checked;
     }
     ```
     And in `combineUrl`: `if (allComponentsSelected.value) files.push(\`${c}/components.css\`);` (was `allSelected.value`).
   - **`docs/.vitepress/theme/components/IconPicker.vue`**: Merged InstUI/Simple Icons into one scrollable list with in-list section headers (`.instui-heading -level-h3 -variant-label` / `-border-top` divider). "All icons" as tri-state master over BOTH sources (`allInstuiSelected`, `allSimpleSelected`, combined `allSelected`/`someSelected`, `toggleAll` sets both `selectedInstui`/`selectedSimple`), disabled until both manifests load (`:disabled="!instuiIcons || !simpleIcons"`) to prevent a race where clicking before the larger Simple Icons manifest loaded silently selected zero Simple Icons. Icon rendering via `-icon-<name>` glyph classes (`InstUiEntry` type shrunk to `{name, source}`). Dark-mode fix: `html.dark .icon-picker__img { filter: invert(1); }` (was `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`). Sizing fix: `.icon-picker__glyph, .icon-picker__img { flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 1rem; width: 1em; height: 1em; }` plus `margin: 0;` on `.icon-picker__img` (overriding VitePress's `.vp-doc img` default margin) and removed hardcoded `width="16" height="16"` HTML attributes. Uses `PickerOutput.vue` for output. Deep-linking via `i_instui`/`i_simple`/`i_fmt`/`i_q`, with async-aware restore (`pendingInstuiSel`/`pendingSimpleSel` read at setup, applied inside `loadInstui`/`loadSimple` once each manifest resolves via `restoreSelection(raw, allNames)` helper).
   - **`docs/.vitepress/theme/components/WebComponentsPicker.vue`** (new file, iterated heavily): Lists all 30 `<instui-*>` elements (hardcoded `ELEMENTS` array — copied, not imported, from the source, since the source has raw CSS imports plain Node can't load and the compiled dist isn't guaranteed to exist at docs-build time). Hardcoded `NESTED_DEPS` map and `withNestedDeps()` helper (mirrors the now-exported source version). Hardcoded `iconElementNames = ["icon", "calendar", "date-input", "drilldown", "rating"]` (mirrors `ICON_ELEMENTS`). Added `DEPENDENCY_ORDER = ["calendar", "date-input", "date-time-input"]` + `orderForCombine(names)` helper for building correctly-ordered jsDelivr combine URLs. Tri-state "All elements" checkbox via `useIndeterminateCheckbox`. Deep-linking via `w_sel`/`w_fmt`/`w_q`. Current script logic (most recent state):
     ```ts
     const needsIcons = computed(() => {
       if (selected.value.size === 0 || allSelected.value) return true;
       return withNestedDeps(selected.value).some((name) => iconElementNames.includes(name));
     });

     const tokenLink = computed(() => {
       const c = "npm/@pantoken/css/dist";
       return needsIcons.value
         ? `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/combine/${c}/style.lean.css,npm/@pantoken/components/dist/component-icons.css`
         : "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@pantoken/css/dist/style.lean.css";
     });

     const esmSnippet = computed(() => {
       if (allSelected.value) return `import "https://esm.sh/@pantoken/web-components";`;
       const only = withNestedDeps(selected.value);
       const onlyList = only.map((name) => `"${name}"`).join(", ");
       return `import { register } from "https://esm.sh/@pantoken/web-components";\nregister(customElements, { only: [${onlyList}] });`;
     });

     const iifeScriptUrl = computed(() => {
       if (selected.value.size === 0 || allSelected.value) {
         return "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@pantoken/web-components/dist/web-components.iife.js";
       }
